{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794735261,"nonce":"HLz2AlSzKWmwwBIMLBU3aladONw=","title":"hxn-gpu-vulkan: a Vulkan driver over the ash crate, binding by hxnsl's SPIR-V layout","message":"The second driver library, after hxn-gpu-metal, and shaped like Vulkan: instance, physical and logical device, queues, buffers and images with their memory, descriptor set layouts and sets, pipeline layouts, graphics and compute pipelines, command pools and buffers, render passes or dynamic rendering, fences and semaphores, and a swapchain on the surface hxn-window's raw handles describe (Xlib, Wayland, Win32, Android).\n\nShaders are hxnsl's `spirv()`: the descriptor set is the bind group and the binding the binding, and `LAYOUT` gives each set's layout, so the driver builds descriptor set layouts from it with no reflection at run time.\n\nUnlike Metal, Vulkan does no hazard tracking: the API has to expose barriers and image layout transitions, or the driver has to track them. Decide which before writing it.\n\nrussl writes SPIR-V with naga's default options: ADJUST_COORDINATE_SPACE is on, so Y is flipped in the vertex shader and the viewport must not flip it again; FORCE_POINT_SIZE is off, so point lists need a shader that writes the point size. See d667dd22a44f962f2eca2c80935e8ab157d115dcf6c5fbd4e73efa86844b0d94.\n\nPlatforms: Linux and Windows on desktop GPUs, Android. CI runners have no GPU; lavapipe (Mesa's software Vulkan) runs the checks on Linux.","files":null}]}